WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:31.730
<b>Suddenly Transferred to
Highedge Records</b>

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.190
<i>It was suddenly announced that B-Project's 
contract with Gandara Music has ended,</i>

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.950
<i>and they'll now be working 
with Highedge Records.</i>

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:36.760
<b>Suddenly Transferred to
Highedge Records</b>

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:44.120
<b>Information Express
Gogodori</b>

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.240
<b>The Mysterious Transfer Announcement</b>

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.810
<i>We're conducting street interviews 
on this breaking news.</i>

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.130
<i>What? No way.</i>

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.130
<i>What?</i>

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.070
Tsubasa, what about Yashamaru-san?

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.130
Um... He didn't answer his phone.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.460
I'll try calling President Daikoku.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.720
<i>I'm sorry for the trouble.</i>

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.390
<i>I'm calling about B-Pro's transfer.</i>

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.600
Yeah. That was quite the announcement.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.680
<i>What?</i>

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.280
I had heard it was happening, 
but I was still surprised.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.410
You knew? Who told you?

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.380
<i>Who? Yashamaru-san, of course.</i>

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.230
What?

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.870
<i>He said it may cause some inconvenience 
at first, but it's best for B-Pro.</i>

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.130
<i>Sumisora-kun? What's wrong?</i>

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.870
<i>Did he not tell you?</i>

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.130
No. I-I'll call back later.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:43.880
<i>If President Daikoku knew, 
then Shuji-san was probably told, too.</i>

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.770
<i>What's going on? 
Am I the only one who didn't know?</i>

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.630
<i>Why?</i>

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.900
Tsubasa-chan, are you okay?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.150
Yes.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.910
The rest of you should wait at the office.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.660
I'll head there later.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.070
Sumisora.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.010
Got it, Sumisora-san.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:16.880
He's not answering.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.550
<b>Yashamaru Sakutaro</b>

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.970
I'll have to try them one at a time.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:34.020
<i>I know a couple places that have 
relationships with Yashamaru-san.</i>

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.020
<b>Kikuchi Art Studio  Funakoshi
Kishida Production  Naganuma 
Kiss & Hug  Yoko Suzuki
Kitada Office</b>

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.780
It's me.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.780
<i>Sumisora-san?</i>

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.520
Yes. Thank you for everything 
you've done for us.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.470
<i>You've got quite a lot going on, don't you?</i>

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.070
I'm sorry for any trouble I've caused.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:50.290
I'm actually looking for Yashamaru.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.900
What? Yashamaru-san's not there?

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:59.300
<i>No. Ma'am, do you have any idea 
where Yashamaru-san might be?</i>

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:04.050
<i>Well, he did take me to a few places.</i>

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.260
<i>If those will do, I can email you a list.</i>

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:07.760
Thank you.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.360
<i>Have the members come 
to terms with the transfer?</i>

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.450
Well...

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.570
I understand. I'll see what I can find, too.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.120
Ma'am...

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.810
<i>Stay strong.</i>

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.830
<i>You're B-Pro's A&R.</i>

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:26.910
I will.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.400
Yashamaru-san.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.280
<i>I thought I just heard Yashamaru-san's voice.</i>

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.660
Yashamaru-san!

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:03.360
<b>Withheld Number</b>

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:10.970
It's Yashamaru-san.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.820
Hello?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.480
<i>Tsubasa-chan.</i>

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.300
Yashamaru-san, I've been looking for you.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:21.650
Why is B-Pro being transferred to Highedge?

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.130
You must be joking, right?

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.360
<i>It's not a joke. It's true.</i>

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.060
But why so suddenly?

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.090
Why didn't you tell me?

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.070
All the members are shocked.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.780
<i>I've been planning it for a while.</i>

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.850
What do you mean?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.730
<i>Well...</i>

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.970
Because I hate you.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.360
Both you and Gandara.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.290
What?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.610
Sir, did you know?

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:57.620
Yes, although I was told Yashamaru-san 
would tell you at the right time.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:03.210
We were only told while you 
were rewriting your new song.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:07.380
But this transfer isn't 
a bad deal for you boys.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.630
Highedge acknowledges B-Pro's talent.

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.550
They've promised to provide total support.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.890
Sir.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:16.890
I'm not just saying this 
to agree with my brother,

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.400
but this is a good chance 
for B-Pro to quickly get ahead.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.730
There's nothing they won't do.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.460
But something's wrong.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.650
Why would we be transferred 
just before our Dome concert?

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:32.490
Not only that, but the news was 
presented in a scandalous way.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.440
And we've been having non-stop 
problems at our jobs recently, too.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:37.660
Yeah.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.630
Like not having makeup artists, and...

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:41.870
The new song.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.410
Could Highedge be involved in that, too?

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:48.670
Yashamaru-san.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.890
You seem well, boys.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.210
Long time, no see.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:55.950
I'm sorry. I've been busy
with what's going on.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:57.810
What's going on?

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.940
I'm the one who masterminded B-Pro's transfer.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.130
Seriously?

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:17.080
Yes. I'm also already an employee of Highedge.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:18.950
What do you mean?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.960
I-I don't get it.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:26.060
Of course. I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.970
Boys, do you remember how your performance

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.810
at the FMJ Music Festival 
was suddenly canceled?

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.550
How could we forget?

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.240
How about the rehearsal troubles 
at the RAIZIN Festival?

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.110
Yes, we remember.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.230
That was actually all Gandara's doing.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.480
What?

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:52.460
B-Pro started with great fanfare, 
but it was difficult in the beginning.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.400
But you know all that.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.520
Some days we had lessons from morning 
until night because we couldn't get any work.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:04.120
I even lost my voice when 
a recording session didn't go well.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.730
Yes, but we still did our best.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.150
We believed that B-Pro would succeed

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:14.010
if we made good music and 
put on good performances.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.200
But the company thought differently.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.520
Gandara planned to withdraw 
from the idol business

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:25.770
just one year after B-Project's debut.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.060
You can't be serious.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.770
After just one year?

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:32.280
Coincidentally, B-Pro quickly 
became a top idol group

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.990
after Tsubasa-chan became the A&R.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:42.040
Naturally, the company changed their 
mind and said they would support B-Pro.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:45.920
But could you trust a company like that?

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:51.420
If we stayed at Gandara, 
my dear B-Pro would've been destroyed.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:57.010
Because I felt that way, 
I began planning your transfer.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:01.430
Highedge can increase 
the scale of the Dome concert.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.880
They're even planning your international debut.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:10.440
They plan to hire the best staff and 
best musicians to write songs for you.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.440
Th-This...

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.190
It's nothing but good news.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:20.080
It sounds like the international debut 
we joked about could become reality.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:24.960
Yashamaru-san, you've been 
working for us this whole time?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.080
Wouldn't Tsubasa-chan be 
happy to hear this, too?

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.710
Totally.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.930
You're on board with this, right?

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:41.180
If it'll make your brand bigger, 
I have no reason to stop you.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.180
Follow your path.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:46.040
Sir.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:54.820
Supporting you as best we can is our job.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.540
It's unanimous, then.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.160
We all agree.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:03.920
For a while?

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.580
Yes, you'll be living here for a while.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.710
But the Japan Dome concert is coming up.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.170
It'll be fine.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:21.270
There's a training room, a pool, 
and a studio where you can rehearse.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:24.140
Order all your meals through 
room service, please.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:27.270
I'll be holding onto your phones.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.680
Even our phones?

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:29.770
Why?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.890
At times like these, it's best if you 
don't read the news about yourselves.

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.700
I can't believe we can't use "Join."

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.110
I won't be able to make any plans for dinner.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.160
We can't even go out in the first place.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:48.160
How? How am I going to see Mamirin now?

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.920
I've already arranged for all your remaining 
jobs to be done here at the hotel.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:56.420
Yashamaru-san.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.090
What about Tsubasa?

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.450
Let me handle her.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:23.310
Yes. I'll be coming by at a later date.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.330
Excuse me.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.080
<b>Kiss & Hug Editor-in-chief 
Yoko Suzuki</b>

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.950
This is Sumisora.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:31.080
<i>It's about Yashamaru-san.</i>

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.290
Yes?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:37.960
<i>He suddenly showed up 
at Gandara Music ten years ago.</i>

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:41.250
<i>But his history before then is unknown.</i>

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.470
Unknown?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:47.470
He was hired mid-term, but I don't 
know through whom he was hired.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.140
<i>I hate to say it, but this is all pretty fishy.</i>

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:56.440
<i>In fact, Yashamaru Sakutaro 
isn't even a real person.</i>

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.190
What?

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.070
<i>A fake name?</i>

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.740
<i><i>So Gandara continued to exploit the members</i></i>

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:09.210
<i><i>without any concern about 
violations of their contract?</i></i>

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:14.330
<i><i>Apparently. I suppose that 
makes Highedge their savior.</i></i>

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.960
<i>That's not true. But why?</i>

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.460
<i>I can't let things end like this.</i>

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:24.470
I won't let them cancel 
the Japan Dome concert.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.560
What's going on, Gandara?

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:34.730
We will hold the concert at the Dome.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.730
Please continue making 
preparations like we planned.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:06.800
<i>Go for what you want. Oh, yeah!</i>

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.750
We're doing great.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:13.390
I hope we can perform 
like this at the concert.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.440
I can't wait.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:18.000
We're really performing at the Dome.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.720
Yeah. It's not a dream.

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:24.140
When Tsubasa said we should aim 
for the Dome, I didn't take her seriously.

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:25.950
But it came true.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:31.620
But we were able to work towards 
that goal because of what Tsubasa said.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:37.870
I felt like it was the first time all ten 
of us were looking towards the same future.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:41.710
Tsubasa really is our wings.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:42.830
What?

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:45.720
At first glance, she seems
weak and unreliable.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:50.160
But she's actually quite flexible.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.250
She turns headwinds into 
strength to fly even higher.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.870
She's B-Pro's wings.

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:04.650
Don't you think it's strange, though?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:08.150
We haven't seen Tsubasa-san for four days.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.630
And tomorrow, we're rehearsing onstage.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:12.950
But we don't have our phones.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.900
We can't get in touch with Tsubasa, 
much less Yashamaru-san.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.470
What about the phones here?

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:23.340
It's no use. It's not connected to the outside.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.050
What do you mean?

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.330
Are we about to follow the wrong path?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.710
My, my, my.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.810
What's wrong, boys? Why so serious?

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:40.080
Yashamaru-san, let us out of here already.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.430
How are preparations 
for the concert coming along?

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.870
There are still things we have 
to discuss with Sumisora-san.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:50.800
Yashamaru-san?

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.830
The Japan Dome concert has been canceled.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:01.730
Highedge has decided 
to let this opportunity go.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.030
I'm sorry.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:07.840
Also, Tsubasa-chan has fled.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.070
What?

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.250
Tsubasa did?

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:14.580
A naïve amateur who couldn't 
tell her left from her right

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.870
was thrown into this industry 
and this situation.

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:22.200
She was scared off by the massive 
responsibility she carried.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.720
What do you think of these lyrics?

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.360
Oh, right. Having your song 
taken from you must've been difficult.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:34.120
We wrote these lyrics together.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.590
I can't believe she made you write lyrics

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:41.750
just because there was 
no time to hire a lyricist.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:44.210
But that won't happen anymore.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.610
You'll have talented staff supporting you.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:54.100
Anyway, I got you something incredible.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:59.770
It's a live morning press conference 
from inside an airplane.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:04.460
Tomorrow, the entire country 
will be talking about B-Pro.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:06.800
A press conference? About what?

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.780
You'll officially announce 
your transfer to Highedge.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:14.840
Then all this nonsense will finally be over.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:15.780
Okay?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:19.540
Did you come up with this?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.210
Of course.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.350
I want to make B-Pro even bigger.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:27.290
I want B-Pro to move the world.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:30.590
I understand.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.240
"Kodo Ambitious?"

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:13.200
This sound...

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:15.050
Could it be?

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.490
Yashamaru-san.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:41.280
Yashamaru-san?

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:46.790
Ten years ago, your father killed my family.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.420
Wh-What are you talking about? 
Besides, my father—

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:56.330
Oh, right. You don't know anything.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:02.100
And your appearance 
really rubs me the wrong way.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.680
So let me tell you.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:09.170
I created B-Pro only 
to make your father suffer.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.190
What?

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:15.690
The spectacular audition and the Bambi 
Training School were tools of my revenge.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:19.550
Has all the trouble that's
happened until now...

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:21.700
The FMJ Music Festival and RAIZIN Festival...

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:24.080
And the Uta Hime Lunch incident...

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.580
Yes. I planned it all.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:28.090
How could you?

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:30.330
They worked so hard on that!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.210
Quiet!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.920
You and Gandara!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:39.970
Everyone who has associated with him and 
everything he's protecting will be destroyed!

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.590
Where is B-Pro?

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:50.270
The members have agreed to the transfer.

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:54.480
Naturally, they know 
they'll get a new A&R as well.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:55.600
What?

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.720
They said they understood.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:02.940
B-Pro's future will continue 
to shine even brighter.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:08.330
And you will suffer in the 
shadows cast by their light.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.290
No. You're lying.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.400
B-Pro doesn't need Sumisora Tsubasa anymore.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:34.060
<b>Aizome Kento
Ashu Yuta
Osari Hikaru
Onzai Momotaro
Kaneshiro Goshi
Kitakado Tomohisa</b>

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:33.610
Guys.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.030
<b>Delivering You Seasonal Information on the Street Corner</b>

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.030
<b>Japan Dome Concert Cancellation 
Causes Bankruptcy 
Danger for Gandara</b>

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:50.290
<i>Boys, are you ready?</i>

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:54.790
<i>The studio's ready for you.</i>

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:56.420
Yes.

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:17.470
No one's here.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.210
No one.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.950
I'm sorry. I...

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:35.680
What?

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.130
Guys.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:48.850
What are you doing here?

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.140
We quit.

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:52.600
We're not going to Highedge.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.600
Though they offered us 
the deal of our dreams...

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.360
None of it appealed to us.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:01.110
After all, you're not there.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:04.570
Sumisora, you're our A&R.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:07.740
You have to keep on being responsible for us.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:11.740
No matter where we performed, 
it wouldn't be fun without you.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:14.370
There's no point if you're not with us.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.630
B-Pro's dreams start on this stage.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:21.630
So let's make the dream we saw 
together come true together, Tsubasa!

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:25.380
G-Guys!

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:32.560
<i>Everything that everyone has 
ever been searching for is here</i>

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:39.150
<i>The moment you take hold of that, 
the revolution begins</i>

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:52.550
<i>I want everything they have 
to reach everyone from this stage.</i>

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:54.500
<i>I want the whole world to hear them.</i>

00:21:54.500 --> 00:22:01.250
<i>Every time we meet, we'll learn a little more</i>

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:07.140
<i>We have nothing to lose, 
our scarred and bruised generation</i>

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:14.020
<i>Closer, farther, and deeper 
to a world we've never seen</i>

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:17.310
<i>Brandishing thousands of swords</i>

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:25.690
<i>Tomorrow will only come 
if we follow this undefined path</i>

00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:30.410
Yes.

00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:34.290
<i>I'll sing out my LOVE, LOVE, LOVE</i>

00:22:33.150 --> 00:22:34.990
<i>What are you doing, boys?</i>

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:42.960
<i>I'll hold your pounding beat in these arms</i>

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:38.460
We're going to follow the path we believe in.

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:39.000
What?

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.630
Bye-bye, Saku-chan.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:46.800
<i>Eternal paradise</i>

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:47.260
<i>Wait. What? What?</i>

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:50.130
<i>It's paradise</i>

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:51.720
<i>You can fly! You can fly!</i>

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:53.220
<i>More and more</i>

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:54.940
<i>You can fly! You can fly!</i>

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:56.430
<i>We'll feel it together</i>

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:57.980
<i>You can fly! You can fly!</i>

00:22:57.980 --> 00:22:59.730
<i>Deeply</i>

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:05.900
<i>Go for what you want. Oh, yeah!</i>

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:14.200
<i>Everything will be changed 
into a brand new world</i>

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:20.040
<i>If you dive in, I'll be waiting 
right there by your side</i>

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:27.130
<i>Everything can be changed 
in our very own story</i>

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:37.770
<i>A beating ambition like no one's 
ever seen that pounds for tomorrow</i>

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:44.360
<i>The unstoppable pounding 
of my heart tingles and throbs</i>

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:50.950
<i>And when it overflows with heart-pounding 
excitement, we'll advance to the next stage</i>

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:01.000
<b>Thanks for Watching!</b>

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:59.350
B-Project will keep on delivering 
their passionate beat to you.
